        "worked_solution": "To solve the inequality \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-8x<0,\n$$\n\nwe need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}-8x\n$$\n\nlies *below* the $x$-axis.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-8x & =0 \\\\ x(x-8) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=0$ and $x=8,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/assets/8c4acb1db29c8479f946d6d047fe79d9a87d7162de1ff0725e59052f93df85ce.png)\n\nThe values marked in blue show all $x$-values where the parabola lies *below* the axis. \n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $0<x<8.$",
